  "theorem": {
    "statement": "Let A_q = (Delta_1^coex)^q on the canonical S^2 coexact carrier. Under metric length rescaling g -> L^2 g, one has Delta_1^coex -> L^(-2) Delta_1^coex, hence A_q -> L^(-2q) A_q. If A_q is to generate primitive line transport parameterized by arclength, it must have inverse-length dimension and therefore must scale as L^(-1). Hence 2q = 1 and q = 1/2. Equivalently, among homogeneous functional-calculus choices of Delta, only sqrt(Delta_1^coex) has the correct dimension for first-order line transport.",
    "principal_symbol_version": "The Hodge Laplacian has principal symbol sigma_2(Delta_1^coex)(x,xi)=|xi|_g^2 Id. A reparametrization-invariant line generator must depend on the cotangent norm |xi|_g, not on |xi|_g^2. Therefore the unique isotropic first-order spectral scale is sigma_1(sqrt(Delta_1^coex))=|xi|_g Id."
  },
